      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "In the past years the bone seeking radiopharmaceutical samarium lexidronam ((153)Sm-EDTMP) has been increasingly used alone or in conjunction with chemotherapy and/or bisphosphonates for the treatment of painful bone metastasis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "Its use has been explored in different solid tumours. In this report we explore its interesting characteristics and describe our experience in multiple myeloma (MM)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "(153)Sm-EDTMP has an affinity for bone and concentrates in areas of bone turnover. It decays as a therapeutic beta-emission and at the same time as gamma-photon that can be used for tracking its concentration with bone scan imaging. Ten patients with symptomatic MM were treated to achieve pain control."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Encouraging results were obtained in MM patients. The use of this radioisotope could be largely improved."
        }
      ]},
